# Express Core

Expert-level Express 5 + TypeScript practices for this API-only project.

## App factory

- `src/app.ts` exports `createApp()` — used by `server.ts` and test helpers
- `src/server.ts` creates HTTP server, listens on `PORT` (default 4000), handles graceful shutdown
- ESM only (`"type": "module"`) — required by Better Auth

## Middleware order (critical)

```text
1. trust proxy (if TRUST_PROXY)
2. helmet + compression
3. CORS (credentials: true, origin: CLIENT_URL)
4. request ID
5. pino-http logging
6. rate limit on /api/auth/*
7. Better Auth handler (BEFORE body parser)
8. express.json()
9. hpp()
10. health routes
11. /api/v1 routers
12. OpenAPI docs
13. not-found handler
14. global error handler
```

Never reorder steps 7–8. See `express-auth.mdc`.

## Graceful shutdown

- Handle `SIGTERM` / `SIGINT` in `server.ts`
- Close HTTP server, then `prisma.$disconnect()`
- Document in `docs/deployment.md`

## Environment

- All config validated in `src/env.ts` with Zod at startup
- Never read `process.env` directly outside `env.ts` (except `vitest.setup.ts`)

## Error handling

- Use `asyncHandler` wrapper for async route handlers
- Global error handler maps `ForbiddenError`→403, `NotFoundError`→404, Zod→400
- No stack traces in production responses

## Type extensions

- `src/types/express.d.ts` — `req.user`, `req.session`, `req.requestId`, `req.activeOrgId`

